-- title:
--   Ostrowski's theorem for rational function fields
-- statement:
--   **Ostrowski's theorem for rational function fields.** Let $K$ be a field and $v$ a discrete valuation of rank one on the rational function field $K(X)$ that is trivial on $K$. Then exactly one of the following holds: $v$ is equivalent to the valuation at infinity $-\deg$, or $v$ is equivalent to the $\pi$-adic valuation for exactly one irreducible polynomial $\pi\in K[X]$ (up to units).
--
--   This is the function field analogue of Ostrowski's classification of the absolute values of $\mathbb Q$. It says that the places of $K(X)$ over $K$ are the closed points of the projective line $\mathbb P^1_K$, and it is the starting point for the theory of function fields of curves and their divisors.
--
--   **Formalization note.** Mathlib's `RatFunc.valuation_isEquiv_infty_or_adic`. `IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum K[X]` is the set of nonzero prime ideals of $K[X]$, each generated by an irreducible polynomial, and `HeightOneSpectrum.valuation` is the associated adic valuation. `RatFunc.inftyValuation K` is the valuation at infinity. `Valuation.IsRankOneDiscrete` says that the value group is infinite cyclic and `Valuation.IsTrivialOn K v` that $v$ is trivial on $K$. `IsEquiv` is equivalence of valuations. `Xor` says that exactly one of the two alternatives holds.
-- source:
--   Listed in Mathlib's curated theorem manifests (docs/1000.yaml); formalized in Mathlib as `RatFunc.valuation_isEquiv_infty_or_adic`. Proof here reduces to that Mathlib result.

import Mathlib

namespace FamousTheorems

theorem ostrowski_rational_function_field_7b {K Γ : Type*} [Field K] [LinearOrderedCommGroupWithZero Γ] (v : Valuation (RatFunc K) Γ)
    [v.IsRankOneDiscrete] [Valuation.IsTrivialOn K v] [DecidableEq (RatFunc K)] :
    Xor (v.IsEquiv (RatFunc.inftyValuation K))
      (∃! u : IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum (Polynomial K),
        v.IsEquiv (IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.valuation (RatFunc K) u)) := by sorry

end FamousTheorems
